# 10-MCR / paid social creative

**Goes here.** The creative itself, on every paid social platform: what the viewer
sees and hears. Hook types, pattern structures, beat sequences, formats, static and
video structure, fatigue, benchmarks, volume by spend, awareness mapping, teardown
method, and analysis of creative that FAILED.

## Not here

- The words: copywriting craft, copy frameworks, persuasion classics -> 11-ADC
- Account structure, scaling, delivery mechanics -> 11-ADC
- Advertorials. An advertorial is a PAGE TYPE -> 07-LPG
- Organic content, including organic short form -> 13-ORG
- A full brand teardown across creative, offers and landers -> 99-multi
- Amazon Sponsored Brands video -> 22-AMZ

**The MCR and ADC line.** MCR is the structure of the creative: which hook, which beat
order, which format. ADC is the words and the machinery that ships it. A "how to write
hooks" source sits on the line; if it is about hook structure it is MCR, if it is
about sentence craft it is ADC.

**Lessons from misfiles.** 8 copywriting books and courses, 1 advertorial blueprint
and 2 brand teardowns were filed here. None were creative structure.

## Platform is a field, not a folder

```
---
url:                   # REQUIRED. Never blank.
rights: public_reference
why:
modules: [MCR]         # add ADC or MEA where it genuinely applies
platforms: []          # meta | tiktok | snap | youtube
topics: []
tier:                  # a practitioner is 3, never 1
scope_hint: growth
---
```

TikTok does not get its own module. A Meta hook works on TikTok with pacing
adjustments, so the knowledge transfers. Tag `platforms: [tiktok]`.

## Topics

hook types, pattern structures, creative fatigue, benchmarks and their samples,
volume by spend band, format and placement, angle versus format, awareness mapping,
teardown method, losing creative analysis, founder ads, VSL structure, static layouts.
`tiktok /` native pacing and sound, trend adjacency and staleness, creator-voice
register, spark and whitelisting.
`meta /` delivery changes and what they mean for creative, including Andromeda.

## Look for

Pattern structures beat by beat. Hook types and when each works. Benchmarks WITH the
sample they came from. Fatigue thresholds. Volume expectations by spend level. The
psychological principle behind each pattern, which is the part that does not go stale.

## Skip

Swipe files with no analysis. AI creative tooling walkthroughs, which decay in months.
A "2027 strategy" published in 2026 is a title, not a date.

## Date discipline matters most here

Half of this has a working life under 12 months. A source with no date is close to
worthless in this folder. Meta's 2025 retrieval changes (Andromeda) mean pre-2025
creative-volume advice needs a re-check.

## Done when

You have 25 to 40 named creative patterns, each with its structure, its works-when
and its fails-when conditions.

